# Playwright Python Test Template

A production-ready [Copier](https://copier.readthedocs.io/) template for web UI test automation with **Playwright**, **pytest**, **Allure**, **Ruff**, and **uv**.

Inspired by the project structure and developer experience of:

- [fastapi/full-stack-fastapi-template](https://github.com/fastapi/full-stack-fastapi-template)
- [yashaka/python-web-test](https://github.com/yashaka/python-web-test)

## Features

- **Playwright** browser automation with `pytest-playwright`
- **pytest** test runner with markers, parallel execution (`pytest-xdist`), and flaky-test reruns (`pytest-rerunfailures`)
- **Allure** reporting with screenshots and page source on failure
- **Ruff** for linting and formatting
- **uv** for fast, reproducible dependency management
- **Pydantic Settings** for environment-based configuration (`local` / `prod`)
- **Page Object Model** examples (and a straightforward style example)
- **GitHub Actions** CI pipeline
- **pre-commit** hooks
- Shell scripts in `run/` for common workflows

## Prerequisites

- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
- [Copier](https://copier.readthedocs.io/) (`uv tool install copier`)
- [Allure CLI](https://docs.qameta.io/allure/) (optional, for local HTML reports)

## Generate a New Project

```bash
copier copy gh:your-org/playwright-python my-product-tests
cd my-product-tests
```

Or from a local clone of this template:

```bash
copier copy /path/to/playwright-python my-product-tests
cd my-product-tests
```

Copier will prompt for:

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `project_name` | Human-readable project name | Playwright Test Project |
| `project_slug` | Python package name (snake_case) | playwright_test |
| `author_name` | Author for `pyproject.toml` | Your Name |
| `author_email` | Email for `pyproject.toml` | you@example.com |
| `python_version` | Python version | 3.12 |
| `base_url` | Default base URL for tests | (empty) |

After generation, Copier runs `uv sync` and `playwright install --with-deps` automatically.

## Quick Start

```bash
cp config.local.env.example config.local.env
./run/tests_smoke.sh
./run/tests_and_allure_report.sh
```

## Project Layout

```text
{{ project_slug }}/
  config/          # Pydantic settings (local/prod env files)
  pages/           # Page Object Model
  support/         # Allure helpers and shared utilities
tests/
  conftest.py      # Playwright + Allure fixtures and hooks
  test_*.py        # Example tests
run/               # Helper shell scripts
config.local.env.example
config.prod.env
pyproject.toml
```

## Configuration

Settings are loaded from `config.{context}.env` files and environment variables.

Copy the example file for local development:

```bash
cp config.local.env.example config.local.env
```

Key settings:

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `CONTEXT` | `local` or `prod` | `local` |
| `BASE_URL` | Base URL for relative navigation | empty |
| `HEADLESS` | Run browsers headless | `false` (local) |
| `BROWSER` | `chromium`, `firefox`, or `webkit` | `chromium` |
| `TIMEOUT_MS` | Default timeout in milliseconds | `30000` |
| `VIEWPORT_WIDTH` / `VIEWPORT_HEIGHT` | Browser viewport | `1440` x `900` |

Inspect resolved settings:

```bash
uv run python -m {{ project_slug }}.config.settings
```

## Running Tests

```bash
# All tests
./run/tests.sh

# Smoke suite only
./run/tests.sh -m smoke

# Parallel execution
./run/tests.sh -n auto

# Specific browser
./run/tests.sh --browser firefox

# With reruns on failure
./run/tests.sh --reruns 2
```

## Linting and Formatting

```bash
./run/lint.sh

# Or directly
uv run ruff check --fix .
uv run ruff format .
uv run pre-commit install
```

## Allure Reports

Tests write results to `allure-results/`. View the report:

```bash
allure serve allure-results
```

Or use the helper script:

```bash
./run/tests_and_allure_report.sh
```

## CI

GitHub Actions runs Ruff checks and smoke tests on push/PR. Allure results are uploaded as artifacts.

## Customization Tips

1. Rename or extend `{{ project_slug }}/pages/` with your application page objects.
2. Add markers in `pyproject.toml` under `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`.
3. Tune `config.prod.env` for CI and remote environments.
4. Keep example tests while bootstrapping, then replace them with your own suites.

